        <name>getResolvedNode</name>
        <qualifiedname>llvm::BlockFrequencyInfoImplBase::WorkingData::getResolvedNode</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Resolve a node to its representative. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Get the node currently representing <ref refid="class_node" kindref="compound">Node</ref>, which could be a containing loop.</para>
<para>This function should only be called when distributing mass. As long as there are no irreducible edges to <ref refid="class_node" kindref="compound">Node</ref>, then it will have complexity O(1) in this context.</para>
<para>In general, the complexity is O(L), where L is the number of loop headers <ref refid="class_node" kindref="compound">Node</ref> has been packaged into. Since this method is called in the context of distributing mass, L will be the number of loop headers an early exit edge jumps out of. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
